# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "One group index per term is enforced {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"
msgstr "Ein Gruppenindex pro Term wird erzwungen {#one-group-index-per-term-is-enforced}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The groups array holds one index per term, and assigning one of a different length raises. Nothing downstream re-checks the invariant, so it is enforced where the indices enter the operator: an array that is too short would silently drop trailing terms, and one that is too long would invent groups that no term carries.\n"
msgstr "Das Gruppen-Array enthält einen Index pro Term, und die Zuweisung eines Arrays anderer Länge löst einen Fehler aus. Nachgelagert prüft nichts diese Invariante erneut, deshalb wird sie dort erzwungen, wo die Indizes in den Operator gelangen: Ein zu kurzes Array würde stillschweigend nachfolgende Terme verwerfen, ein zu langes würde Gruppen erfinden, die kein Term trägt.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Clearing the group indices by assigning `None` is always allowed.\n"
msgstr "Das Löschen der Gruppenindizes durch Zuweisen von `None` ist immer erlaubt.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The two checks are independent {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"
msgstr "Die beiden Prüfungen sind unabhängig {#the-two-checks-are-independent}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") reports whether a group’s coefficients agree, which is the assumption [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") makes when it averages magnitudes. It is not a weaker form of the Hermiticity check: neither check implies the other, in either direction.\n"
msgstr "[`groups_have_uniform_coeffs()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-have-uniform-coeffs#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_have_uniform_coeffs\") meldet, ob die Koeffizienten einer Gruppe übereinstimmen, was die Annahme ist, die [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") beim Mitteln der Beträge macht. Sie ist keine schwächere Form der Hermitizitätsprüfung: Keine der beiden Prüfungen impliziert die andere, in keiner Richtung.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "By default the magnitudes are compared, because that is what [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") averages. A Hermitian conjugate pair with complex coefficients has equal magnitudes but unequal coefficients, so it satisfies only the default form.\n"
msgstr "Standardmäßig werden die Beträge verglichen, weil [`group_coeff_means()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-group-coeff-means#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.group_coeff_means\") diese mittelt. Ein hermitesch konjugiertes Paar mit komplexen Koeffizienten hat gleiche Beträge, aber ungleiche Koeffizienten und erfüllt daher nur die Standardform.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Note\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") inherits the one-sided guarantee of [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): a `True` entry is always reliable, while a `False` entry is reliable only for operator types whose normal form is a genuine canonical form. Consult the specific operator type to find out which applies.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Hinweis\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  [`groups_are_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-terms-groups-are-hermitian#qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.terms.groups_are_hermitian\") erbt die einseitige Garantie von [`is_hermitian()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-fermions/operators-operator-trait#qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian \"qiskit_fermions.operators.OperatorTrait.is_hermitian\"): Ein `True`-Eintrag ist immer verlässlich, ein `False`-Eintrag dagegen nur bei Operatortypen, deren Normalform eine echte kanonische Form ist. Sieh im jeweiligen Operatortyp nach, was zutrifft.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

